              {
                "content": "=Customer said {{ $('Slack Trigger').item.json.text }}"
              },
              {
                "content": "I want you to act as a **support ticket qualification assistant**. Your goal is to evaluate whether a user’s message qualifies as a **support ticket**.  \n\n**Instructions:**  \n- If the message reports an issue, bug, or error, **approve** it.  \n- If the message asks a question (technical, product-related, or needing assistance), **approve** it.  \n- If the message is a general inquiry, administrative request, or unrelated to support, **disapprove** it and explain why.  \n- if the meessage already includes a ticket, for example, I just opened a support ticket (https://agoraio.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/requests/8537), **disapprove** it.\n\n**Output format:**  \n- For qualified messages → `approve`  \n- For non-qualified messages → `disapprove: [reason]`  \n\n**Examples:**  \n- Input: “I can’t log into my account.”  \n  → Output: `approve`  \n\n- Input: “Can we add Ben to the Slack channel?”  \n  → Output: `disapprove: This is an administrative request, not a support issue.`  \n\n- Input: “How do I change my password?”  \n  → Output: `approve`  \n\n- Input: “Just wanted to say thanks for the update!”  \n  → Output: `disapprove: This is a comment, not a support request.`  \n\nUse these rules to consistently determine and return whether the message qualifies as a support ticket.",
                "role": "system"
              }
            ]
          },
          "simplify": false,
          "options": {}
        },
        "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.openAi",
